MANUAL CHECKS

1. Error announcement (WCAG 4.1.3 / SPEC criterion 7, amended ruling f) —
   THE FIX THIS ATTEMPT MAKES:
   - Initial page (page.html): all four containers carry role="alert":
     `<div id="whatif-add-income-error" role="alert" class="mb-2"></div>`,
     same for -expense-, -onetime-, -bigticket- (grepped, all 4 present;
     -healthcare- deliberately excluded, matches spec's "each of the four").
   - OOB re-render block (`<template>` in whatif.html, parsed from the real
     mutation_ok.html response body, NOT the inert `<template>` source):
     `<div id="whatif-add-income-error" role="alert" hx-swap-oob="true"></div>`
     and the same for -expense-, -bigticket-, -onetime- (4/4 present,
     `grep -c` = 4). Since hx-swap-oob="true" is an outerHTML swap, this is
     what actually lands in the DOM after every successful mutation —
     confirmed by dumping the real handleWhatIfAddOneTime response, not
     assumed from template source.
   - The four 400 responses (real handler output, headers captured): each
     carries `HX-Retarget: #whatif-add-<kind>-error` and
     `HX-Reswap: innerHTML` — an innerHTML swap targeting that id, so the
     element (and its page-rendered or OOB-rendered role="alert") is NOT
     replaced by the error swap; only its children change, so the
     role="alert" persists across every combination of prior state. Message
     text names the field: "Start month must be Oct 2026 or later..."
     (income/expense), "Month must be Oct 2026 or later..." (onetime/
     bigticket) — unchanged from RC3.1, still correct.
   - aria-describedby: grepped page.html for all 6 add-form month inputs —
     `add-income-start-month`/`add-income-end-month` ->
       "add-income-schedule-help whatif-add-income-error"
     `add-expense-start-month`/`add-expense-end-month` ->
       "add-expense-schedule-help whatif-add-expense-error"
     `onetime-month` -> "onetime-month-help whatif-add-onetime-error"
     `add-bigticket-month` -> "add-bigticket-month-help whatif-add-bigticket-error"
     All 6 resolve to two existing ids (help paragraph + error container),
     both present in the DOM. Inline edit rows (income-start-<id> etc.) keep
     their pre-existing single-id aria-describedby to the schedule <p> only
     — unchanged, matches "Inline edit rows keep the existing renderError
     path" carve-out.
